<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6063"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 2:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dr. Kelleher&#39;s profile is the one I follow but for amateur kicks: <BR> <BR>&#42; An absolute liar. <BR>&#42; No remorse. Didn&#39;t kill Vian kids because he didn&#39;t want to be perceived as a child killer - not for any moral reason but for sake of &#34;image.&#34; <BR>&#42; Otero was his first murder&#40;s&#41;; expected Julie to be alone and had fantasized her as such. <i>Unexpectedly finding the kids made him angry and skewed his fantasy;</i> enraged at his mistake, took it out on the kids and Mr. Otero; assumed Mr. Otero was dropping off older kids at school <i>on his way to work; didn&#39;t know Mr. Otero would be driving back home;</i> bad reconnaissance of Otero family routine; <i>didn&#39;t even know that Josephine and Joseph II existed before the actual attack, thought the older kids were the only kids.</i> <BR>&#42; Did not know any victims. They were random, including Mr. Otero. <BR>&#42; Very patient. <BR>&#42; Knows every nook and cranny of Wichita. <BR>&#42; Carries a gun when in public, at least when making drops. While unlikely, may have applied for a permit to carry a concealed weapon; one can only hope that this has been checked out. <BR>&#42; Has but one fear: capture. Doesn&#39;t intend to be taken alive, hence the firearm. However, his fear of capture is a far cry from overwhelming. <BR>&#42; A military buff, emphasis on WWII. Favorite military personage, Patton.  <BR>&#42; Was never an active serviceman or police officer <BR>yet knows extensive information about each. <BR>&#42; While the word is overused it applies; he is a narcissist. <BR>&#42; Trusts <i>no one</i> but will never be significantly paranoid. <BR>&#42; Sexually dysfunctional, possibly a virgin. <BR>&#42; Considers himself &#34;self-taught.&#34; <BR>&#42; Would go out of his way to tell people, &#34;I&#39;m not a joiner.&#34; <BR>&#42; His mention of something as obscure as The Panty Hose Strangler in Florida indicates not only an interest in detective magazines but implies a nearly omniscient awareness of serial killers. He needed to be considered The Authority about anything. His use of the word &#34;we&#34; to link himself with the serial killers in the same letter further underscores his cry for attention. <BR>&#42; He began communicating last March primarily due to the mention of a book about him. <BR>&#42; He will be extremely difficult to capture. <BR> <BR> <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
